  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Durable hand-off",
      "items": [
        "The API writes queued jobs into PostgreSQL. The worker polls and claims leased rows, then checkpoints and persists stage results.",
        "The represented hand-off is database-mediated; this path contains no direct API-to-worker RPC."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "External calls",
      "items": [
        "Brave search and the configurable HTTPS chat-completions adapter run from worker stages when configured.",
        "Company pages are fetched through the public-URL guard; the diagram does not imply these providers are currently live."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Human approval gates",
      "items": [
        "Preparation approval is separate from delivery: email delivery requires an approved draft, an enabled and verified sender, then a separate approve-send action.",
        "The worker hands off SMTP only for a queued delivery attempt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundary",
      "items": [
        "Compose config gives the dashboard an API base URL, while API and worker use distinct database identities; PostgreSQL has no published host port in this stack.",
        "This marks credential separation, not a claim that the Compose network enforces service-level ACLs."
      ]
    }
  ]
